<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Drawing an inequality step by step</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>You are going to show {@id@} on a grid, shading the unwanted region.</p><p>(a) The boundary line crosses the \(x\)-axis at \(x =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>(b) It crosses the \(y\)-axis at \(y =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p><p>(c) How should you draw the line, and which side should you shade?</p><div>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The boundary is {@lind(a, b, c)@}. (a) Put \(y = 0\): \({@a@}x = {@c@}\), so \(x = {@X@}\). (b) Put \(x = 0\): \({@b@}y = {@c@}\), so \(y = {@Y@}\).</p><p>(c) The sign is {@sconcat("\\(", relt(rel), "\\)")@}, so [[if test="strictp(rel)"]]points on the line are not included: draw it dashed.[[else]]points on the line are included: draw it solid.[[/if]] Test \((0, 0)\): \(0 {@relt(rel)@} {@c@}\) is [[if test="osat"]]true, so \((0, 0)\) is in the required region \(R\), which we leave clear. Shade the side that does not contain \((0, 0)\).[[else]]false, so the side containing \((0, 0)\) is unwanted. Shade it, and \(R\) is the other side.[[/if]]</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
